code: 0
--- stdout
Process from .github/dojo.toml (preset kanban): board acme/3, issues in acme/shop, acme/api.
Run a verb as gh dojo <verb> <N>; --dry-run shows its plan first.
Every command takes --json (schema_version 1), --jq and --template, as gh does.

Verbs:
  start       берёшь задачу в работу
              optional --comment; warns about unresolved blockers; comments "Взял в работу. Сессия: {session} {comment}"
  wait        Work is stuck: waiting for another issue or an outside decision
              needs --by or --comment; --by N also marks it blocked by #N; comments "Waiting for {by}. {comment}"
  done        The change is released
              several numbers at once (done 12 13 14); optional --comment; also on closed issues; comments "{comment}"; closes as completed
  note        Leave a progress note without moving the issue
              needs --comment; comments "Progress: {comment}"
  park        Put the issue back

Every verb adds the issue to the board if it is missing and refuses a
closed issue unless noted. A repeat is safe: an effect already in place
(status, comment, labels, assignee, blocked-by link, closed or open) is
skipped.

Lifecycle (from → to):
  start       Backlog, Waiting, Ready → In progress
  wait        In progress → Waiting
  done        Ready, In progress → Done; closes as completed
  note        any status → status unchanged
  park        any status → Backlog
  Initial:    Backlog (new issues; also an issue with no status or not on the board)
  Final:      Done (gh dojo list hides it unless --all)
  Resolved:   Done (a blocker in these no longer blocks)

Exit codes:
  0  everything applied: go on
  1  bad arguments or config: fix them as the error says
  2  a process check refused: don't work around it; ask the user
  3  issue or board not found: check the number (gh dojo list) or board.owner/project in .github/dojo.toml
  4  network, rate limit or auth: retry later, or gh auth refresh -s project
  5  partially applied: re-run the same command; it finishes the rest
  A verb on several issues (batch) exits 0 when all are done, 5 when some were
  written and a re-run may finish the rest, else with the code of the failed
  ones (2 first, then 1, 4, 3); a summary names each issue not done.
--- stderr
